.staging/*
!.staging/README.md
node_modules/
# Paper PDFs stay local-only: the public repo must not redistribute publisher-copyrighted
# documents. The catalog ledger (.reference/catalog/REFERENCES.md) records identifiers and
# digests so every file is independently re-fetchable.
.reference/papers/*.pdf
# Personal Claude Code overrides (machine-specific)
.claude/settings.local.json
# Vendored corpus bytes: never committed - the committed artifact is
# experiments/parser-census/corpus-manifest.json (pins, licenses, counts).
corpus/
# Root-level PDFs. The .reference/papers rule above states the policy — the
# public repo must not redistribute publisher-copyrighted documents — but only
# covered one directory, so a PDF dropped at the root slipped the net.
/*.pdf
# Local credential scratch. Ignoring is CONTAINMENT, NOT SECURITY: the bytes
# are still in the working tree in plaintext. The fix is to hold secrets
# outside the repo (or in the keychain) and rotate anything that has sat here.
/turso_tok.md
